        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This behavior is further supported by the ablation study in Table VIII. Removing uncertainty weighting (i.e., using fixed equal weights) causes the species loss to dominate optimization, leading to reduced ultra-rare accuracy (63.8% → 61.5%) and slightly degraded segmentation quality (Barbel IoU: 32.9% → 32.6%). These results highlight that dynamically prioritizing more stable tasks effectively mitigates noise in fine-grained, long-tailed biological data.",
